WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Difficulty Level: King of Diamonds

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.200
Game: Impostor

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:16.000
All teams will be assigned one of two roles:
HUMAN... or IMPOSTOR

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
There can be more than one Impostor
per round

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.500
A computer science word will be revealed
to all human teams

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.000
The word will NOT be revealed
to the IMPOSTOR team

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The HUMAN teams must correctly identify
the impostor.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The IMPOSTOR must conceal their identity
and deceive all others.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Teams will proceed individually
in an assigned order

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Each team must submit a phrase,
no longer than THREE words.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:57.000
The phrase must be related to the given word.
It is strictly prohibited to directly input the given word.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:05.200
Your phrase will be judged, analyzed,
and questioned by other teams

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:16.700
Additionally, all teams, both human and impostor teams,
have the liberty to interact with the lotus flower during their turn
for a hint on the assigned word.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:26.800
However, interacting with the flower alerts all teams in the game
during your turn, and drains the life of the lotus flower
as well as the surrounding environment.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:39.500
The lotus flower can only be used ONCE
during your team's turn, meaning teams know you've used
the hint to your advantage and can become suspicious.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:46.000
After all responses have been submitted,
all teams must vote for a suspected Impostor

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Alternatively, teams can vote for an additional round,
with the same roles and term

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:00.500
The votes are tallied by the game system,
and the identities of each player are then revealed
to all screens

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.000
If the IMPOSTOR team is correctly identified,
all HUMAN teams are rewarded 2 points
for the duration of the game.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:17.700
However, if the IMPOSTOR team survives,
the IMPOSTOR team is rewarded 5 points
for the duration of the game.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:25.800
The point distribution marks the end of one round,
starting a new round with different roles
and different words

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.400
The game will last for 3 rounds.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:36.000
By the end of the 3 rounds, the three team(s)
with the highest amount of points
receives a GAME CLEAR

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.000
All other teams will receive a GAME OVER

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:47.700
The IMPOSTOR game tests the extent
of your Computer Science knowledge,
as well as your ability to read or hide from others

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.000
The game will now begin.